  "model_envelope": "The HEM mass flux spans -65 % to +5 % of the measured mass flux across the nine recorded nozzle points. Points 1 to 4 fall inside the reported +/-2 sigma band and points 5 to 9 fall outside it. No correction was fitted to close that gap, so the five failures stand as the edge of the model.",
  "not_benchmarked": [
    "Nucleation delay, metastable flashing and phase slip; the model is homogeneous and at equilibrium throughout.",
    "Discharge-geometry effects beyond the user-supplied discharge coefficient.",
    "Real-fluid compressed-liquid behaviour; the liquid branch carries one density and an incompressible pressure correction.",
    "Browser/Python parity, which needs a Python runtime and is not re-run in the page."
  ],
  "notes": [
    "Every recomputed figure here is produced by calling window.__dgcBenchmark() on the tool, so any verdict in this record can be reproduced by opening the page.",
    "At the critical temperature the property routine returns rho_f = 325.2364 kg/m3 and rho_g = 318.7049 kg/m3 against rho_c = 322 kg/m3 (1.005 % and -1.023 %), because waterTsat clamps pressure to p_c(1 - 1e-6) before inverting and the saturated densities vary as tau^(1/3). Only the saturation pressure is graded at that point.",
    "The critical-point search is graded in benchmarks/two_phase_critical_flow.json, which drives the same HEM core; it is reported without a verdict here to keep each case to a single criterion."
  ]
}
